name 'ai-and-algorithmic-decisions-postassessment-q6_2026'

question 'A quiz app calls the same set of steps every time a user submits an answer: check the answer, update the score, show feedback, load the next question. Why would a developer put those steps inside a function?'

wrong 'Functions make the page load images faster.'
right 'A function lets the developer write the steps once, give them a name, and reuse them by calling the function every time an answer is submitted.'
wrong 'Functions are required for any app with more than one question.'
wrong 'Functions automatically detect when a user is cheating.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

